I'm not sure they are up to

02:43.760 --> 02:49.440
the job on on their own. Our
food is being produced in a way
that has devastating
consequences

02:49.440 --> 02:54.840
for the environment, for social
justice, and for our individual
health. In less than a

02:54.840 --> 03:01.040
generation, it has been
industrialized and globalized.
Processed food is routinely
adulterated

03:01.040 --> 03:07.680
with artery clogging fats, a
besegenic sugars and
constipating starches, which are
then disguised

03:07.680 --> 03:12.920
by chemical colorings and
flavorings without which they
would be unpalatable. We have
come

03:12.920 --> 03:18.760
to depend on this junk food, and
it is making us sick. On
nutritionally depleted diet

03:18.760 --> 03:25.200
is now kneeling on par with
tobacco as the cause of ill
health and premature death.
Manufacturers

03:25.200 --> 03:30.360
use these raw materials instead
of good quality fresh food,
because enormous subsidies

03:30.360 --> 03:36.760
mostly paid by Western taxpayers
have made them cheap. About 70%
of the value of the US

03:36.760 --> 03:41.560
soy of being comes from the US
government, no wonder soy of
derivatives are found in

03:41.560 --> 03:47.600
two-thirds of all processed
foods. Subsidized US corn is
turned into ubiquitous corn

03:47.600 --> 03:53.080
sweeteners and modified starches
for the same reason. The money
made from food is shifted

03:53.080 --> 03:57.720
from those at the bottom of the
chain, the farmers and
producers. To those at the top,
the

03:57.720 --> 04:03.200
tiny number of big transnational
food processors, manufacturers
and retailers who control

04:03.280 --> 04:09.680
our food as never before.
Protectionist subsidies have
done little to save farmers who
are going

04:09.680 --> 04:14.960
out of business everywhere. The
value of agricultural
commodities on which so much of
the

04:14.960 --> 04:20.320
developing world depends for its
livelihood has slumped. As other
barriers to trade have

04:20.320 --> 04:26.560
been removed, inequalities in
wealth have grown. Half the
world now stars for lack of food

04:26.560 --> 04:32.240
while the other half suffers
from diseases of excess. The
money made from these
commodities

04:32.320 --> 04:37.840
is concentrated in the hands of
the cartels that control trade
in them. Just five giant

04:37.840 --> 04:43.920
coffee manufacturers control
over half the world's coffee
beans. Ten years ago coffee
producing

04:43.920 --> 04:49.920
countries kept 30% of the retail
value of the coffee we buy.
Today they keep just 10%.

04:50.720 --> 04:56.960
When we buy a jar of instant
coffee, we pay 7,000% more than
the farmer got for it.

04:57.840 --> 05:03.680
These concentrations of power
are repeated across the food
chain. Some 45% of grain trade
is

05:03.680 --> 05:10.480
controlled by one US company,
Cargill. The power of
transnational manufacturers is
mirrored by

05:10.480 --> 05:16.240
the emergence of dominant food
rate retailers. In the near
future, just four of five
retailers

05:16.240 --> 05:22.240
will have one global domination
with a handful of others
dominating regionally. Three
quarters of

05:22.240 --> 05:27.360
grocery sales in the United
Kingdom are in the hands of four
supermarket groups. They have a

05:27.360 --> 05:33.600
stranglehold on how our food is
made and distributed. They've
created a system that is in its
use

05:33.600 --> 05:38.880
of new information technology
and logistics, both miraculous
and impossibly destructive.

05:39.680 --> 05:44.640
Thanks to the barcode, food is
flown around the world to meet
the supermarkets requirements
for

05:44.640 --> 05:51.360
just in time ordering. Their
demand for cosmetic perfection
and a perpetual global summer

05:51.440 --> 05:56.880
can be met by producers only if
they use agrochemicals
intensively and allow for a

05:59.280 --> 06:06.480
big fucking word, degree of
waste. A third of canyon green
beans are thrown away because
they are the

06:06.480 --> 06:11.920
wrong size or shape. This new
business model has made the
supermarkets highly profitable,

06:11.920 --> 06:18.960
but it depends on the extraving
it use of that most politically
charged and polluting of
substances

06:19.040 --> 06:25.440
crude oil for the food miles,
for the pesticides, for the
packaging that makes up 40% of
our domestic

06:25.440 --> 06:31.040
waste. It depends on an endless
supply of cheap outsourced labor
that can be turned on and off
like

06:31.040 --> 06:36.240
a tap. Hundreds of thousands of
migrant workers now live in
Britain in conditions that would
make

06:36.240 --> 06:42.480
Dickens blush. The way we eat is
not just ecologically
unsustainable, but also morally

06:42.560 --> 06:48.960
and even biologically
unsustainable. Making it better
requires radical structural
change.

06:48.960 --> 06:54.080
It needs tighter competition
policies, it needs reform of
subsidies and trade rules,

06:54.080 --> 06:59.440
it needs regulation of business
none of which government is
inclined to do. So making our
food

06:59.440 --> 07:05.120
